  lesson: "Honesty",
  ages: "For everyone",
  mins: "6 min read",
  summary: "In a crowded market, a cloth merchant uncovers a hidden tear in his finest fabric — moments before a wealthy buyer offers him a fortune for it.",
  moral: "Honesty in earning is not the enemy of profit — it is the foundation that trust, and blessing, are built upon.",
  ref: "The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ praised “the truthful and trustworthy merchant”, who will be with the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs. (Reported by al-Tirmidhi)",
  body: [
      "There was, in a busy market town, a cloth merchant named Hasan whose shop was the smallest on his street and whose name was the largest. People said: “If Hasan says the cloth is pure wool, you may buy it blindfolded.”",
      "One morning, unrolling a bolt of his finest silk for the day’s display, Hasan’s fingers found what his eyes had missed in the dim storeroom: a tear, no wider than a thumb, hidden deep in the folds where only a careful hand would ever feel it. His young brother shook his head. “Sell it quickly, before the flaw is found. Every merchant in this market would do the same.”",
      "That very afternoon, a wealthy trader from a distant city entered the little shop, looking for silk worthy of a governor’s household. He held the bolt to the light and named a price that would have fed Hasan’s family for half a year.",
      "Hasan was silent a moment. Then he unrolled the cloth further, found the tear, and laid it open on the counter. “Before you pay,” he said, “see this. I will not sell you a flaw in the dark and call it silk in the light.” The trader stared — not at the tear, but at the man. Then he paid the full price, took the cloth, and made Hasan his supplier for twenty years, saying: “A man who hides nothing from me will hide nothing in his accounts.”",
      "Years later, when Hasan’s shop had grown and his sons asked him the secret of it, he smiled. “Once,” he said, “I sold a torn cloth in the open, and with it I bought a name that has never torn since.”",
      "For another market story about trust when an easier profit appears, read <a href=\"#waqiat\" data-related data-related-kind=\"waqiat\" data-related-idx=\"4\">The Merchant’s Word</a>.",
  ],
