  summary: "Hasan and Umar inherit their father's field and must divide it between them. The elder brother quietly gives the younger the better half by the river — and the younger, troubled by the gift, secretly carries sacks of his own grain to his brother's store at night. When the secret comes out, both brothers discover that fairness is not about counting grains, but about wanting for your brother what you want for yourself.",
  title: "Islamic Story About Fairness in the Family: The Two Brothers and the Divided Field",
